---
import PublicLayout from '../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';

const origin = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_URL?.replace(/\/$/, '') || Astro.url.origin;
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: origin + '/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Terms & Conditions', item: origin + '/terms' },
    ],
  },
];
---

<PublicLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions — Using Media Reservoir"
  description="The terms for using Media Reservoir: free to use, end-to-end encrypted, your files stay in your own storage, no warranty, and your responsibilities — including safeguarding your password and recovery key."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="legal-page">
    <PageHero eyebrow="Legal Document" title="Terms & Conditions.">Last updated: June 20, 2026</PageHero>
    <div class="container-sm">
      <div class="legal-content">
        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>1. Agreement to Terms</h2>
          <p>
            By creating an account or otherwise using the Media Reservoir service (the "Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions. If you do not agree to these terms, do not use the Service. Media Reservoir is free and open-source; the source code is also licensed separately under the AGPL-3.0 license.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>2. What Media Reservoir Is</h2>
          <p>
            Media Reservoir is a free, end-to-end encrypted gateway for storing media in cloud storage you own. Your files are encrypted in your browser and sent directly to your own storage bucket; we operate only a thin control plane that holds an encrypted index. We never store your files, your encryption keys, or your storage credentials, and we have no technical means to read your media.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>3. Your Responsibilities</h2>
          <p>
            Because the Service is end-to-end encrypted and uses storage you control:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>You are solely responsible for safeguarding your password and your recovery key. We cannot reset them, and if you lose both, your encrypted data is permanently unrecoverable — by design, there is no backdoor.</li>
            <li>You are responsible for the cloud storage account you connect, including its costs, security, durability, and backups. Your files live in your storage, not ours.</li>
            <li>You agree to use the Service only for content you have the right to store, and not for any unlawful purpose or in violation of others' rights.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>4. Fair Use & Limits</h2>
          <p>
            The Service is free and provided on a fair-use basis. To keep it sustainable, we may apply reasonable limits (such as the number of items or total index size per account) and may suspend accounts that abuse the Service or attempt to disrupt it. Because your files are stored in your own bucket, such limits affect only the metadata index we host on your behalf.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>5. No Warranty</h2>
          <p class="warning-text">
            THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR OPERATORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SERVICE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SERVICE.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>6. Your Content</h2>
          <p>
            We do not access, collect, index in readable form, parse, or transmit your media. The content of your files never reaches our servers — only ciphertext you generate and an encrypted index do. You retain absolute ownership of all your files, and we have no mechanism to view, scan, or recover them.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>7. Changes to Terms</h2>
          <p>
            These terms may be updated from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by the "Last updated" date above, and your continued use of the Service after a change constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>8. Contact Information</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions about these Terms, you can contact the project maintainer at <a href="mailto:fantasyfalcoon91@gmail.com">fantasyfalcoon91@gmail.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PublicLayout>

<style>
  .container-sm {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px;
  }

  .legal-page {
    padding: 0 0 96px;
  }
  .legal-page > .container-sm {
    padding-top: 60px;
  }

  .legal-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 32px;
  }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .legal-section p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-body);
  }

  .legal-section ul {
    margin-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-body);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .warning-text {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    background: var(--bg-inset);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 16px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .legal-section a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .legal-section a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-hover);
  }
</style>
